## 3. Automated Danger PR Bot Verification

The **Danger PR bot** runs as the final step in the Bitrise CI pipeline, analyzing pull request metadata, static analysis findings, and code coverage numbers before posting an actionable review comment:

```ruby
# Dangerfile
# Enforce PR description length
fail("Please provide a meaningful PR summary explaining your architectural changes.") if github.pr_body.length < 30

# Check for tests on modified business logic
has_source_changes = git.modified_files.any? { |file| file.start_with?("src/main", "Sources/") }
has_test_changes = git.modified_files.any? { |file| file.start_with?("src/test", "Tests/") }

if has_source_changes && !has_test_changes
  warn("This PR modifies core application code without corresponding test modifications.")
end

# Check SonarQube / JaCoCo coverage report
jacoco_report = "app/build/reports/jacoco/jacocoTestReport/jacocoTestReport.xml"
if File.exist?(jacoco_report)
  coverage = parse_jacoco_coverage(jacoco_report)
  if coverage < 80.0
    fail("PR Code Coverage is #{coverage}%, which fails the mandatory 80% threshold.")
  else
    message("PR Code Coverage: #{coverage}% (Exceeds 80% threshold)")
  end
end
```

