## 5. Step 3: Configure Bitrise Secrets &amp; Steps

### 5.1 Store Sauce Labs Credentials in Bitrise Secrets

In Bitrise &gt; **Workflow Editor &gt; Secrets Tab**, declare your API credentials:
* `$SAUCE_USERNAME`: Your Sauce Labs account username.
* `$SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY`: Your Sauce Labs alphanumeric access key (found under User Settings &gt; Access Key).

### 5.2 Add Steps to `bitrise.yml`

Integrate the two steps into your `deploy-staging-qa` workflow:

```yaml
# 1. Register App in Sauce Labs Storage
- git::https://git.enterprise.internal/mobile-engineering/bitrise-step-sauce-labs-app-create.git@v1:
    title: Sauce Labs App Create
    inputs:
    - yaml_file_path: "saucelabs.request.yml"
    - sauce_username: $SAUCE_USERNAME
    - sauce_access_key: $SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY

# 2. Upload Compiled Binary & Execute Tests
- git::https://git.enterprise.internal/mobile-engineering/bitrise-step-sauce-labs-upload-and-test.git@v1:
    title: Sauce Labs Mobile Upload and Test
    inputs:
    - sauce_username: $SAUCE_USERNAME
    - sauce_access_key: $SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY
    - sauce_region: "us-west-1"
    - app_path: $BITRISE_APK_PATH
    - app_name: $SAUCE_APP_FILE_NAME
    - test_command: "saucectl run --config .sauce/config.yml"
    - working_dir: $BITRISE_SOURCE_DIR
    - test_fail_on_failure: "yes"
```

